 "title": "Levi, Moses and Aaron",
 "ref": "Exodus 6:14–25",
 "col": "japheth",
 "intro": [
  "Placed between God's commission to Moses and his first meeting with Pharaoh, this genealogy shows who Moses and Aaron are: Levites, four generations from Jacob. It begins with Reuben and Simeon, the two older brothers, and then dwells on Levi, naming the clans that will serve at the tabernacle and the priestly line of Aaron to Phinehas."
 ],
 "sources": "Hebrew names: Miqra according to the Masorah. Rashi on Exodus 6; Mekhilta; Babylonian Talmud, Sotah 12a and Bava Batra 109b. Scholarly summary after the standard commentaries.",
